    "notes": "The exact Wilfredor CC0 native confirms Notre-Dame’s broad gray-limestone Gothic facade, paired tall square towers with crenellated crowns/corner pinnacles, two tiers of louvred pointed openings and round rose panels, three upper statuary niches, triple recessed entrance/arcade and lower paired side lights. Current whole, front, portal, statuary and crown renders retain these identifying forms. Seasonal blue light meshes, snow, trees and street fixtures are excluded. Low main roof, hidden nave/side/basement geometry and fine stone/tracery/figural profiles remain medium-fi architectural estimates. The rear Sacred Heart chapel, seminary and interiors remain excluded."
